From d9f9a0076af0dfcd64f675eac006547d73b29483 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <root@your.mom>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:53:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Retire native-id inputs before score and selection reductions

Upstream-base: native-input source da925efbc8, after candidate-38 and selected-logit source c88a692e98.

Rationale: native id pointers and dynamic strides otherwise stay live across register-heavy reductions. Gather selected values into the existing score output before normalization for noncompact ids, and write native sampled top-k columns before selection. Compact int64 inputs retain the original kernel form, selected without a copy. Compact int64 score arithmetic remains unchanged.

Quality: no extra allocation, dtype/layout materialization, precision change or change to score ordering and ranks. Each selected value is stored as the same FP32 value that the final arithmetic consumed before.

Tests: full numerical/native-layout/graph/prompt/speculative checks and controlled interleaved performance qualification required. This change is not performance-qualified yet.

Upstream-status: local candidate, not submitted upstream.
---
 tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_tilelang_topk_ids.py |  3 +-
 vllm/v1/worker/gpu/sample/tilelang_logprob.py | 16 +++++++++-
 .../v1/worker/gpu/sample/tilelang_topk_ids.py | 32 +++++++++++++++----
 3 files changed, 43 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

